  "decision_conditions": [
    "The following specification was granted in 2019. To maintain consistency with that approval, the Council is permitting the same specification as an alternative to the currently proposed works:\r\n\r\n'T1 – Cedar – Reduce lateral growth by up to 1m (MAXIMUM) and crown thin outer canopy by 10–15% on the roadside of the tree. Reduce lateral spread by up to 2m (MAXIMUM) and crown thin outer canopy by 10–15% from over the owner’s property and neighbouring property to allow space for greater canopy development. No height reduction is permitted with this specification.'\r\n\r\nPlease note: crown thinning involves the selective removal of branches to reduce canopy density and improve light penetration and air flow. It does not include any reduction in the overall height of the tree."
